WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.620
A change in sediment supply or depositional conditions creates

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:07.780
a different layer. Bedding records these changes. Read the

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:11.220
boundaries and the material inside each bed before interpreting

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:16.040
the sequence. A sediment-bearing flow weakens. Coarser grains settle

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:19.560
first, then finer particles accumulate above them. The resulting

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.800
bed fines upward. This is a graded bed; it

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.760
records a change during deposition within one bed. Wind

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.600
or water carries grains up a bedform and deposits

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:32.280
them on the down-current slope. The bedform moves while

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:35.940
inclined laminae accumulate and are partly truncated. These are

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:39.560
cross beds. They record deposition and migration, not a

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:40.840
later fold of every layer.
